Dataset: German national team matches and tournament finals, UEFA Euro 2016
through FIFA World Cup 2026.

Provenance: Derived from the openfootball project
(https://github.com/openfootball/worldcup and
https://github.com/openfootball/euro, CC0-1.0), which explicitly waives EU
sui-generis database rights. WC-2026 knockout slot times sourced from the
official FIFA match schedule as published on Wikipedia (kickoff facts, not
copyrightable).

Row-selection rule: every match involving the German national team plus every
tournament final, UEFA Euro 2016 to FIFA World Cup 2026.

Window rule: [kickoff − 30 min floored to the hour, kickoff + D + 60 min
ceiled to the hour], where D = 120 min for group-stage matches and 165 min for
knockout matches.

Provisional rows (provisional = 1): WC-2026 knockout slots are recorded at
fixed slot times with unresolved team placeholders (E1_PATH, E2_PATH). These
rows are used by the provider identically to resolved rows and may be revised
when the bracket is finalised.
